    },
    {
      "text": "Hf addition will form a stable, adherent Hf-rich oxide scale.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "CoCrFeMnNi bond coats without reactive-element additions typically form less-adherent oxide scales during high-temperature cycling.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf-modified bond coat will develop a continuous oxide scale.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf-rich oxide scale will grow slowly.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf-rich oxide scale will have high adherence to the bond coat.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "During high-temperature exposure, Hf will segregate to the alloy/oxide interface.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf segregation at the alloy/oxide interface will anchor the oxide scale.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Interfacial anchoring by Hf will diminish oxide-scale spallation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Interfacial anchoring by Hf will reduce oxygen ingress.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced spallation and oxygen ingress will slow degradation relative to an untreated CoCrFeMnNi bond coat.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf-alloyed bond coat will exhibit less oxide spallation than the untreated bond coat under cyclic oxidation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hf-alloyed bond coat will degrade more slowly than the untreated bond coat under cyclic oxidation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed beneficial mechanism will remain effective at 0.5–1 at.% Hf and 1100–1200 °C in corrosive cyclic-oxidation environments.",
